<http://data.silknow.org/object/af1437ae-a58c-320f-89dd-912a19006975/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Dark blue silk playbill with gold lettering with the programme for the evening reproduced within an ornate printed gold border, headed with the royal crest and surrounded by the words Theatre Royal Haymarket, Last Night of the Season. Produced for the benefit night of the lessee Mr. Benjamin Webster, 15 January 1840, and featuring details of the evening's programme comprising Edward Bulwer Lytton's play <i>The Sea Captain, or, the Birthright</i>;  the farce <i>His Last Legs,</i> a farewell address and the farce <i>Our Mary Anne</i>. Printed with the names of the casts for the plays: Mr J. Webster, Mr. Strickland, Mr Macready, Mr Howe, Mr O. Smith, Mr Phelps, Mrs Warner, Miss P. Horton, Mr Power, Miss Travers, Mr Buckstone, and Mr T.F. Mathews."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/af1437ae-a58c-320f-89dd-912a19006975> .

